  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_018: multimodal/multiprofile/scgpt/ViT-L/transformer/weighted → acc 0.52, 2.86 GPU hrs), evidence is very sparse. The most important uncertainty is whether the expensive multiprofile + transformer aggregation pipeline is actually contributing to accuracy, or whether a simpler singleprofile setup with the same strong encoders (scgpt, ViT-L) and weighted fusion achieves comparable performance. Config_001 (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, None, weighted) isolates this question by removing aggregation and multiprofile while keeping the core multimodal fusion. Expected cost is roughly 1.2–1.6 GPU hours (no transformer aggregation, single profile), significantly cheaper than config_018. If it matches or approaches 0.52, we save substantial compute for the remaining 8 experiments and can focus on tuning the cheaper singleprofile space. If it drops substantially, we confirm multiprofile + transformer aggregation is essential and should exploit that direction. This is the highest-information, cost-efficient next step under the limited budget."
}

